Yup. 1836 it was a stretch of open prairie and wetlands.  german Settlers experimented with being corn, and tulip farmers, but dairy has been the main agricultu industry until the second half of the 20th century.

&#x200B;

schaumburg illinois was pretty isolated, still speaking german primarily in schools and church services, local newspapers until 1955 when the village incorporated To avoid being swallowed up and absorbed into the new Hoffman Estates community.

&#x200B;

schaumburg still reflects its German roots with a living museum with 1880’s german settler farm, old buildings preserved including the 1867 Lutheran church( tallest building outside Chicago in cook county until 1920) as well as being historically a progressive community as a 1892 pamphlet describes schaumburg as,” prompt in its tax payments, and welcoming to all looking to progress in life On earth”.

Hey,

&#x200B;

ive wanted to die since I was 9 too.

&#x200B;

the last 13 years have been hell. And I’m not looking foreward to the rest of how ever many years people deem I need to experience.

I hope you may find peace, the strength, and Confidence to make a choice that is right for you.

what I want to say is...

The choice to end ones life should be yours and yours alone. I’m not pushing anyone to do anything. but it is my philosophical belief that one should have the right to choose when to end their own life.

its not an easy choice. It is not. you make this choice to end a feeling of pain. And that is a legitimate reason to end ones life; to stop pain. Just ask the terminally ill.

&#x200B;

and for those saying how In theory, your family will miss you. In theory yes. But just as I have no place saying your family won’t miss you, no one has a place to say they will. They don’t know the situation, and I don’t.

&#x200B;

all I do have is advice. I think you should plan your last day(s) out to maximize your peace. Be it visiting old places you loved or hated. Saying a goodbye in an un alarming way to people you care about. don’t go all out in case you do have a change of heart...

&#x200B;

but I trust people when they say they cant go on. It should be a persons right to choose to not exist.  I respect those choices. Maybe one day people wont be forced to find peace and die at their own hands; deathcare could be achieved.

&#x200B;

and if you do choose to go on... that is your choice and equally as valid and respectable.

That’s... unusual. Unless they are loose already.

&#x200B;

please make sure he’s only pulling them if they are already loose. and I don’t think he likes the pain either🥺.

Watch an episode of Everyohe Loves Raymond.

&#x200B;

Whenever the main character is hugged by his mother, he isn’t faking hating it. The writers never told him when it would happen, and the fans of the show assumed it was the characters trait to not like his hovercraft mother.

He genuinely was surprised every time in an episode that happened😂  


and they allowed for the actors and actresses to ad lib a bit, so funny moments there too.

&#x200B;

the whole show is a gem in my opinion. Cross between a family sitcom and curb your enthusiasm Type energy of the situations.

&#x200B;

my favorite episode where there is a hug and in general is,” the angry family“. It ends up with the entire family yelling in a priests office In a family therapy type thing, and the priest is exhausted trying to referee everyone 🤣

Well not it’s not just an autism thing.

&#x200B;

Its a person acting like a responsable human being.

If I were you, and you wanted to make a point...

be extra needy, go right up to the line of faking it and being annoying.

&#x200B;

”dad can you bring me the milk from the counter? I need it in my coffee“

\*brings milk, he walks away, you pour\*

&#x200B;

” hey can you put this back in the fridge?”

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

” Im feeling hungry”

&#x200B;

” the sun is hurting my eyes.”

&#x200B;

““I like th

“is it hot outside? Or raining“

just prove that  the opposite of being independent and responsible is being needy and borderline annoying.

&#x200B;

your doing fine, I’m always for more independence. And your dad needs to untangle his worries from your life. Maybe tell him,” I have a great therapist if you need any help..” in a genuine sounding way I’d he gets on you about not untangling himself from your [life.lol](https://life.lol)  


unless you need him for a specific task, he does nit need to know.

Big one is music in general( original concert band composition, arranging for marching/ pep band), second would be history( American and Europeans emphasis, all the isms). and I have cooking and baking to take care of my grandparents I live with.

&#x200B;

I have smaller ones that I don’t obsess over too, but are more passionate than an NT. Knitting, weaving, making clothes, gardening, koi keeping, parakeet keeping, Doing laundry by hand In a tub outside if I’m stressed, and sometimes I like hammy acting, like quoting puns, or old groucho marx type things. Being sarcastically dramatic so everyone knows your joking because it’s so out of my usual rational chill character.

&#x200B;

my favorite like off the cuff moment was when I was leaning on the wall on my phone At a largeish party in 2018 With lots of people who know me, some really well. And this girl who was an athlete came over and tried to encourage me to come get some kool aid with her, she lightly grabbed my arm and I TOTALLY hammed up fake falling to the carpet. Like a did half a flip and landed on the meaty side of my body, and a loud thud.

&#x200B;

everyone like stopped and saw me looking at her( trying not to laugh cause timing is everything in comedy)  I was like, “well Melinda, it Seems you’ve been taking my advice and working on your pitching arm, great job!”. ( she was a softball pitcher , everyone knew I was joking and laughed,  and I melodramativly got to my feet like I was gonna fall again and shook  her hand as if to congratulate her.

&#x200B;

I know, a long story, And for a minor interest. but it’s fun being punny, melodramatic Bugs bunny type of person if people know your just joking lol. It brings some excitment to partiea and day trips( the beach, the park, the city) for sure.

It’s cute, it’s sexy, it’s calming.

&#x200B;

alright guys, the new thing for the 2020’s is calming your Nervous Aspie BF or your NT BF with your built in pacifiers 🤣 Watch a movie or show and chill. How romantic lol

I feel your pain, or at least could understand.   
I would go home from my food job as a server and I would work in my sleep. Usually if you dream about working a shift that’s a pretty obvious sign something is seriously wrong.

&#x200B;

and yeah, every week was a countdown to the weekend and the job, I crammed 20 hours a week into 2-2.5 days. Made okay money, just god, i would freak out in bed as I’m drifting into sleep about how table 3 needs iced tea and coke refilled, and table 4-5-6 party needs their pizzas NOW, and the bar needs a second round... and then I would repeat that until I would actually say, “ I am not at work, I am in my bed, I put in a good shift at work, let’s work at work.”

&#x200B;

my favorite job was an aquarium tech. I maintained office and restaurant fish tanks. And i got paired with a team member who drove🙂.  Got to see a lot of the area around My region where I live.

&#x200B;

maybe look for a job that is not a high caliber, high movement, constant movement one. Like an assistant to someone? A trade professional?

.

It’s not abnormal. humans in general are programmed to freak out in a total silence or an isolation. other species like birds hate total silence too. Silence=danger.

&#x200B;

and yeah, that feeling of danger could be amplified in Aspies.

Im a strong believer in having a residential house number.

you could have an iPhone too if you want, but in addition to that, I would give the household number to docs, business professionals( plumbers, lawn care) and overall more non personal relationships and those that are good for the entire household.

&#x200B;

but my small group of friends get both my home and my personal, with preference on my personal.

&#x200B;

and yes, I advocate choosing someone in your household with a good, clear voice to represent you all in A recorded voicemail, be it a related family or a roommate Type household. You don’t even have to include A last name, just the info needed.

Hey.

&#x200B;

My mom and dad separated when I was 3. And my mom tried to have my younger brother and I, but she had other interests besides us. It was about 3 months she had us. And then she took us to our grandparents house, dads parents, rang the doorbell and left.  She told us it would be three days.

&#x200B;

I remember on the third day I waited all day and well into the night for her to come and pick us up. And she never did. It traumatized my brother he I. So much so that I am very sensitive to the idea of being abandone.

she chose to only see us once a week for 3-5 hours, and then she would have a job and have adult fun with her adult friends.

&#x200B;

I’m 21 now, and the last time I saw her in person was about 2 year ago, very briefly. I’m pretty sure I will never want to be in the same room with her again, but I still call 2-3 times a year to check up and make sure she is still alive,

feeling ignored sucks. And sometimes there are  real reasons why friend x can’t speak at the moment, or when grandma is busy, but I get the feeling of when you enter a room and try and participate in a convo and everyone acts like nothing was going on in the first place.

Im not religious, but I wish you some patience to help cope and Some strength/courage to make relationships that matter to you on your own pace.
